{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":4,"prev":"be179b8d755280a17d8c44b37c5cf80ce0f03c256635b79651361f3e1493f935","at":"2026-09-28T07:21:55.368341Z","type":"node_output","state":"discover","iter":0,"node":"discover","data":{"output":{"findings":[{"tag":"bug","file":"internal/repo/worktree.go","start_line":56,"end_line":57,"issue":"With a bare main worktree RunStoreRoot falls back to RootOr(start), the linked worktree status runs in, so discoverAbandonedRuns' unattributable-run rule (here == main) is true in every worktree and an abandoned run whose worktree was removed becomes a MustClear blocker in all of them.","consequence":"In the bare+worktrees layout #174 enables, removing a worktree that left an FSM run at a non-terminal node makes status exit 1 and the Stop hook block in every other worktree, and the run cannot be advanced because its work dir is gone.","confidence":70,"severity":"P2"},{"tag":"advisory","file":"tests/go/test-bare-layout.sh","start_line":1,"end_line":4,"issue":"The bare-layout test drives a single linked worktree only; no second worktree reads the shared store, and the removed-worktree case is not covered.","consequence":"A regression in cross-worktree store sharing or removed-worktree reporting in a bare layout would not be caught.","confidence":60,"severity":"P3"},{"tag":"advisory","file":"internal/fsm/cli/wiring.go","start_line":120,"end_line":137,"issue":"In a bare layout the anchor (RepoRoot) is whichever linked worktree runs the command, but the storeRoot block comment and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md still say the anchor is the main worktree.","consequence":"Readers are told the anchor is always the main worktree; per-worktree anchors surprise them.","confidence":60,"severity":"P3"}]}}}
